cff-version: 1.2.0
title: AquaSolDB
message: >-
  If you use this dataset, cite it as below AND cite the original paper that
  printed each value you use; the `source_id` column of every row names that
  paper, and `csv/sources.csv` gives its full reference and DOI.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Abdulsalam
    family-names: Abd
    affiliation: Hamad Bin Khalifa University
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9536-5988
version: "1.0"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22870466
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A curated collection of published experimental measurements of gas solubility
  in water and brines, with companion tables for water content of gas and
  hydrocarbon-liquid phases, gas-mixture solubilities and phase-boundary points.
  22,872 measurement rows from 496 sources, read from rendered images
  of the printed pages, normalised to common units beside the value as printed.
keywords:
  - gas solubility
  - brine
  - hydrogen
  - carbon dioxide
  - methane
  - nitrogen
  - hydrogen sulfide
  - light hydrocarbons
  - water content
  - phase boundaries
  - experimental data
# R-DB3-23: the `doi:` above is the CONCEPT DOI, the address that always resolves
# to the newest version; the two entries below name the same concept DOI and the
# VERSION DOI of this release, which is the one to cite for a number taken from it.
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22870466
    description: The concept DOI of the dataset (all versions)
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22870467
    description: The version DOI of AquaSolDB v1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/abdul-salam94/AquaSolDB"
date-released: "2026-09-20"
preferred-citation:
  type: dataset
  title: AquaSolDB
  version: "1.0"
  doi: 10.5281/zenodo.22870467
  authors:
    - given-names: Abdulsalam
      family-names: Abd
      affiliation: Hamad Bin Khalifa University
      orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9536-5988
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  notes: >-
    Citing this dataset does not replace citing the source of a value. For any
    number you use, cite the paper `source_id` names as well.
